  "id": "Compound::DB00530 - Gene::1558",
  "verbalization": "Erlotinib is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c8 through a series of interconnected pathways. The evidence suggests that Erlotinib causes Hepatorenal Syndrome, which is triggered by Mefenamic Acid, and that Mefenamic Acid binds to Cyp2c8. Similarly, Erlotinib causes Obliterative Bronchiolitis, which is associated with Amiodarone, and Amiodarone also binds to Cyp2c8. These findings collectively indicate that Erlotinib may influence Cyp2c8 through the binding of its metabolites, which are themselves linked to the enzyme. The lowest common ancestor of these pathways is the Organooxygen Compound, suggesting a shared biochemical mechanism. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Erlotinib in modulating Cyp2c8 activity via its metabolites, underscoring a dependency on the enzyme in the context of these pathological conditions.",
